n-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/39afbdbf-870a-4720-a8f6-e9e8bd9d26aa/eede803f-c7b3-4539-b041-157fea5c26f9" class="r-2vy5r1" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="65388ed4-3b51-4e32-9ff4-fef019dd60b6" class="r-gwo9ck"><div data-rid="d83f88dd-0873-4ad4-bbb4-36c6ad920742" class="r-14yfkv7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Frequently Asked Questions</p></span></div><div data-rid="2fe05ec9-d2e5-409d-aba0-19954aa562d6" class="r-2cp1rx" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="c3452821-c343-4087-9cae-49af50c6e812" class="r-wb8qti" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="open" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="e0418a25-841f-4c5d-9831-50569ca2a686" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="replo-:R6n32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-fonyv2 r-z1thld"><div data-rid="a9f977e3-26b4-4d1f-8beb-c99ae6db14f4" class="r-171ndq7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What are the Tuttle Twins books about?</p></span></div><div data-rid="249e5b27-5cb0-419d-934c-7c124f6af429" class="r-1fuvwta" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-ck39ue" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4 8a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h7a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-7A.5.5 0 0 1 4 8"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" id="replo-:R6n32:"><div data-rid="bfe45bd1-17a8-40d3-a807-4d199a95adb8" class="r-1r8efg3"><div data-rid="cc508cfe-d0dc-4c85-8337-c9cc4233ba40" class="r-1uz0280 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span>The Tuttle Twins books teach kids about timeless principles—like freedom, critical thinking, and personal responsibility—through engaging, age-appropriate stories. Instead of memorizing facts, children discover these ideas by following fun adventures, relatable characters, and real-world examples.</span></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="dd0e3973-f3b9-44bc-9b7c-085afaa0f733" class="r-1e0dhxc" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="feecbc5d-63f5-4fa8-864b-8422a0f0bea2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Ran32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1p7cr14"><div data-rid="8b9473ce-7d2e-479c-b912-17b9920fbd26" class="r-1q3nrbv alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>What ages are the books for?</p></span></div><div data-rid="92bd3ba3-a07c-455f-8783-3aa9fc18422c" class="r-eydxzx" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-axzsvj" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Ran32:"><div data-rid="fa66e6dd-1bc7-436d-a613-8bd52ea3e7fe" class="r-18oyu5x"><div data-rid="02932c42-dc92-4664-8782-19055e67d4e9" class="r-pcyyvn alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>We have books for every stage of your child’s development:</p><p><strong>Ages 0–4:</strong> Board books with colorful illustrations and simple ideas.</p><p><strong>Ages 5–7:</strong> Picture books with short, engaging stories.</p><p><strong>Ages 8–12:</strong> Chapter books that explore deeper concepts.</p><p><strong>Ages 13+:</strong> Teen and young adult books with more advanced discussions.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="ebcda68a-e90d-470c-8140-60ace12dd463" class="r-ln7ax0" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="1d983e8a-310b-4009-8dd0-20e13f3308fe" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Ren32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-jliujy"><div data-rid="752fb118-ac37-42eb-bd0b-8afdabd56512" class="r-o070xw alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Do my kids need any prior knowledge to understand these books?</p></span></div><div data-rid="21d52556-b66b-4ef9-ada1-0515e0472e18" class="r-9tjvc9" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-2ayppd" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Ren32:"><div data-rid="1a3d5512-2e03-469d-b26f-6feaa480318a" class="r-agwj1b"><div data-rid="333c0a65-af13-460e-9641-f4c85e57ae81" class="r-12t0gmi alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span>Not at all! Each story starts from scratch, making it easy for any child to understand—whether they’ve heard of these ideas before or not. The books are written to make learning feel like play, so kids naturally remember what they’ve learned.</span></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="2083ff47-6efe-4cbd-9cf1-c97a7888f872" class="r-14dqxcu" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="a6db7185-7e5b-47d8-bef7-f48db6c145c3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rin32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-kybrb6"><div data-rid="72099326-63f4-494a-bd8c-830b301f7bc1" class="r-1l45fh7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>How do these books compare to school textbooks?</p></span></div><div data-rid="f721fc84-0561-46b5-a9d3-6ba81f60b654" class="r-5eqsjp" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-c0mcbl" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Rin32:"><div data-rid="e2cfb379-bef9-4f41-826e-72b83a0763f2" class="r-dk7fho"><div data-rid="531675c4-b7e1-4331-9d68-f0fd7014cafb" class="r-1f6d98 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><span>Unlike most textbooks, the Tuttle Twins use storytelling to make learning effortless and memorable. Research shows kids recall and understand more when lessons are woven into an engaging story rather than presented as dry facts.</span></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="773fb13b-ed44-44d4-b3f6-67a8d5c367d8" class="r-1k769tl" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-rid="84a55116-50c2-4987-9bbe-95d324353e78" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="replo-:Rmn32:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1iagqv3"><div data-rid="5eb80b39-d389-40b1-af2b-b39fd213079e" class="r-treia9 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Where should I start if I’m new?</p></span></div><div data-rid="07efc434-d5e6-4b81-a930-aab54c81a63d" class="r-1g5ejy3" aria-hidden="true"><svg stroke="currentColor" fill="currentColor" stroke-width="0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand" style="width:var(--rsw, 100%);height:auto;max-height:100%" class="r-1a5lhcr" height="1em" width="1em" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M8 4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v3h3a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-3v3a.5.5 0 0 1-1 0v-3h-3a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1h3v-3A.5.5 0 0 1 8 4"></path></svg></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:Rmn32:"><div data-rid="70f4a1c7-6c8d-4fe6-95e9-8d9320469683" class="r-1fa3bfu"><div data-rid="1765d136-6963-4f37-ba26-d8ab4903246e" class="r-171tzhf alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Start with the set that matches your child’s age:<br><strong>Ages 0–4:</strong> Begin with the Tuttle Toddlers Combo Set — colorful board books that introduce big ideas in a fun, simple way.<br><strong>Ages 5–12: </strong>Go for the Family Starter Pack — a mix of storybooks that spark curiosity and help kids apply important principles.<br><strong>Ages 13+:</strong> Jump into the Teen & Beyond Bundle — thought-provoking reads that challenge older kids to think critically and engage with the world around them.</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
